\par\b\fs30 1. Executive project state\b0\fs22\par
\par
PDF Studio is an independently branded PDF platform under active development. The current product is a working prototype, not a finished commercial service.\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 Authorized scope\b0\fs22\par
\par
Only Stages A-D are authorized:\par
\par
- Stage A: engineering foundation, safety, isolation, CI, reproducibility.\par
- Stage B: core PDF utilities and document conversions.\par
- Stage C: viewer and professional editor capabilities.\par
- Stage D: OCR, signing, secure redaction, advanced/professional operations.\par
\par
Stages E and F are frozen. Do not implement AI PDF chat, AI summarization, AI translation, subscriptions/billing, user accounts, enterprise organizations, collaboration, cloud document history, or large automation platforms unless the owner explicitly changes scope.\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 Current implementation snapshot\b0\fs22\par
\par
On main at the beginning of the PPTX milestone, PDF Studio had:\par
\par
- FastAPI backend.\par
- pypdf-based PDF toolkit.\par
- 15 prototype tools including DOCX-to-PDF.\par
- Basic HTML/CSS/JavaScript frontend.\par
- Internal processing worker.\par
- Gotenberg 9 conversion service.\par
- Docker Compose deployment.\par
- Pytest and GitHub Actions.\par
- Playwright browser smoke tests.\par
- Upload validation/resource limits.\par
- Private worker/Gotenberg network.\par
\par
The PPTX milestone is implemented in open PR #19, which raises the tool count to 16 tested prototype tools when merged.\par
