\par\b\fs30 6. Primary upstream research decision\b0\fs22\par
\par
Exactly two primary repositories were selected.\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 6.1 Gotenberg\b0\fs22\par
\par
- Repository: https://github.com/gotenberg/gotenberg\par
- Selected release: v9.5.1\par
- Tag commit: 2a025609d36eb7a970c31397e652ee439a7214fe\par
- Project license: MIT\par
- Role: private server-side Office/document conversion.\par
- PR #19 tested container:\par
  gotenberg/gotenberg:9.5.1@sha256:a0f596c2aeee6391c24ccf2953737971f13976b14d4240525a447f209185e2c8\par
\par
Why selected:\par
\par
- Already integrated and working for DOCX.\par
- LibreOffice route handles DOCX/PPTX/XLSX and other Office formats.\par
- One stable HTTP boundary is simpler than a second converter backend.\par
- Existing worker/network/test architecture can be reused.\par
- No reason to replace working pypdf operations.\par
\par
Do not:\par
\par
- Copy Gotenberg's Go server into PDF Studio.\par
- Expose Gotenberg publicly.\par
- Accept arbitrary user-supplied conversion URLs.\par
- Enable arbitrary remote document retrieval without a new security review.\par
- Add another converter for the same feature without benchmark evidence.\par
\par
Runtime/license caution:\par
\par
Gotenberg's MIT license does not automatically cover the entire container. The exact image includes separately licensed runtime components such as LibreOffice, Chromium, Debian packages, fonts and other dependencies. Production redistribution needs image-level license/SBOM/security review.\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 6.2 Mozilla PDF.js\b0\fs22\par
\par
- Repository: https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js\par
- Selected release: v6.5.438\par
- Tag commit: 0a4153349dc473ba950fc17941c5ca7eda43c1de\par
- License: Apache-2.0\par
- Role: Stage C browser PDF viewer/workspace foundation.\par
- Current status: selected/researched, not yet integrated.\par
\par
Initial Stage C reuse targets:\par
\par
- High-quality PDF rendering.\par
- Page thumbnails.\par
- Page navigation.\par
- Zoom.\par
- Text selection.\par
- Text search.\par
- Rotated/mixed-size pages.\par
- Responsive layout.\par
- Keyboard interaction/accessibility.\par
- Future annotation UI foundation.\par
\par
Do not claim PDF.js provides arbitrary high-fidelity underlying-PDF-text rewriting.\par
\par
Self-host audited PDF.js assets. Do not send local preview PDFs to a third-party CDN/service.\par
\par
