\par\b\fs30 7. Why other repositories are secondary\b0\fs22\par
\par
PUBLIC_PDF_REPOSITORIES.txt is the full study catalog.\par
\par
General conclusions:\par
\par
- pdf-lib / Konva / pdfme: possible targeted Stage C helpers, not replacements for Gotenberg/PDF.js.\par
- OCRmyPDF: strong Stage D OCR specialist.\par
- pyHanko: strong Stage D signing/validation specialist.\par
- qpdf / PDFBox / pdfcpu: useful only when a demonstrated gap exists; avoid unnecessary duplicate engines.\par
- PDFClear / Folio: study UX/editor interaction patterns; do not merge entire applications blindly.\par
- Commercial SDKs such as Apryse/Nutrient: only for separate native-text-editing research with owner approval, license/cost analysis and proof of real underlying-content modification.\par
- Do not introduce AGPL, noncommercial, source-available or paid SDK components into the intended proprietary product without explicit owner approval/license review.\par
