\par\b\fs30 8. PPTX-to-PDF milestone - implementation record\b0\fs22\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 API\b0\fs22\par
\par
POST /api/tools/pptx-to-pdf\par
\par
Input: one PPTX file.\par
Output: validated downloadable PDF.\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 OOXML/PPTX validation\b0\fs22\par
\par
PR #19:\par
\par
- Retains the 8 MiB input limit.\par
- Requires ZIP/OOXML structure.\par
- Requires [Content_Types].xml.\par
- Requires ppt/presentation.xml.\par
- Requires the exact PowerPoint main content type.\par
- Rejects a DOCX renamed to .pptx.\par
- Rejects invalid ZIP/non-PPTX archives.\par
- Bounds entry count.\par
- Bounds total declared expanded size.\par
- Bounds per-entry expansion.\par
- Bounds compression ratio.\par
- Rejects unsafe/duplicate archive paths.\par
- Rejects encrypted OOXML archives.\par
- Does not extract the OOXML package to the filesystem.\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 Gotenberg request restrictions\b0\fs22\par
\par
- Fixed trusted route: /forms/libreoffice/convert.\par
- No user-provided converter URL.\par
- Environment proxies disabled.\par
- Redirects disabled.\par
- Public converter hostnames rejected by PR #19.\par
- Compose service name/private literal addresses permitted.\par
- No parallel conversion backend.\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 Output validation\b0\fs22\par
\par
Converted output must:\par
\par
- Have application/pdf response MIME.\par
- Start with a PDF signature.\par
- Parse strictly with pypdf.\par
- Be unencrypted.\par
- Have 1-200 pages.\par
- Stay <= 40 MiB.\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 Error model\b0\fs22\par
\par
- Invalid input / converter rejection -> sanitized 422-class response.\par
- Temporary Gotenberg/network failure -> sanitized 503 with retry semantics.\par
- Converter-unavailable category survives API -> worker -> child boundaries.\par
\par
\par\b\fs26 Frontend\b0\fs22\par
\par
The existing no-build frontend:\par
\par
- Shows PowerPoint-to-PDF.\par
- Accepts PPTX.\par
- Explains current limits.\par
- Converts/downloads.\par
- Shows meaningful errors.\par
- Can reuse resulting PDF in another tool.\par
- Remains usable at mobile widths.\par
- Does not migrate the app to React.\par
\par
